window.EXAMS=[{"id":"P1-2017-20","paper":1,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"20","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"income elasticity of demand data for coffee (+2.0) and tea (-0.5) provided in question","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"A café sells two types of hot drinks. These drinks have the following income elasticities of demand: \nCoffee: income elasticity of demand +2.0; Tea: income elasticity of demand -0.5 \nThe volume of coffee sales is several times greater than the volume of tea sales. \nBased on the information above, analyse how the café's overall sales volume of hot drinks would be affected by a rise in consumers' incomes. Assume there are no other changes."},{"id":"P1-2017-21","paper":1,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"21","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"Figure 5","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Use the data in Figure 5 to explain how the use of debt factoring would benefit ABC Ltd. \nFigure 5: Extracts from the balance sheet of ABC Ltd. 31.3.2015 (£000) / 31.3.2016 (£000) / 31.3.2017 (£000): Inventories 200 / 230 / 250; Receivables 300 / 500 / 690; Cash 400 / 200 / 0; Total current assets 900 / 930 / 940; Payables 500 / 530 / 550"},{"id":"P1-2017-22","paper":1,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"22","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"A business wants to increase the productivity of its workforce. To what extent is the greater use of delegation likely to be an effective way for the business to achieve this?"},{"id":"P1-2017-23","paper":1,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"23","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"A business has recently started to use Elkington's Triple Bottom Line to assess its overall performance. To what extent do you think the business is likely to have lower profits as a result of this?"},{"id":"P1-2017-24","paper":1,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"24","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"A business has had a record of poor innovation for many years. To what extent do you think that if the business increases its investment spending on innovation this will lead to more success in this area?"},{"id":"P1-2017-25","paper":1,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"25","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"A business is experiencing a fall in its market share. To what extent might the greater use of digital technology enable the business to increase its market share?"},{"id":"P2-2017-01.3","paper":2,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"01.3","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"Figure 6","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"The discount retailers are said to manage their human resources very effectively. Explain how the data in Figure 6 supports this view. Use calculations to support your answer."},{"id":"P2-2017-01.4","paper":2,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"01.4","marks":20,"type":"16d","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"To what extent do you think the 'big four' supermarkets should change their strategies and adopt the discounter model?"},{"id":"P2-2017-02.2","paper":2,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"02.2","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse the likely effects of a significant increase in interest rates on the profits of car manufacturers."},{"id":"P2-2017-02.3","paper":2,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"02.3","marks":16,"type":"16o","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Many car manufacturers are expected to respond to a fall in overall capacity utilisation in the industry by cutting prices. To what extent is cutting prices a good way for any business to respond to a fall in the overall capacity utilisation in its industry?"},{"id":"P2-2017-03.1","paper":2,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"03.1","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"Figure 7","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"A manager from the UK is moving to South Africa to lead a team of local staff. Explain how the difference in Hofstede's cultural dimension of 'Power Distance' shown in Figure 7 might affect her management style."},{"id":"P2-2017-03.2","paper":2,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"03.2","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"Figure 8","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"With reference to Figure 8, analyse the actions Kento should take regarding its product portfolio in Europe to improve its long term financial performance."},{"id":"P2-2017-03.3","paper":2,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"03.3","marks":16,"type":"16o","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"To what extent is Africa an attractive market for all businesses wanting to sell their products internationally?"},{"id":"P3-2017-01","paper":3,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"01","marks":12,"type":"12","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse, with reference to Kotter and Schlesinger's work, two barriers to change that KMH plc will face when implementing its new strategy."},{"id":"P3-2017-02","paper":3,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"02","marks":12,"type":"12","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse, using two financial ratios, the financial constraints faced by KMH plc in attempting to fund the new strategy."},{"id":"P3-2017-03","paper":3,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"03","marks":16,"type":"16","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"KMH plc uses a soft approach to Human Resource Management. Using the information provided, assess whether KMH plc should change its approach to Human Resource Management to help boost its profit."},{"id":"P3-2017-04","paper":3,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"04","marks":16,"type":"16","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"To analyse its competitive environment in the cruise ship engine market segment, KMH plc uses Porter's five forces model. Use the information provided to decide whether the power of buyers or the likelihood of new entrants is the bigger threat to KMH plc."},{"id":"P3-2017-05","paper":3,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"05","marks":20,"type":"20","needs":"the case study, Table 2 in Appendix C","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Most journalists blamed the fall in KMH plc's profits on either a failure to control costs or a slowdown in the growth of the global economy. Which of these two reasons do you think is the main cause? Justify your answer using information from the case study and Table 2 in Appendix C."},{"id":"P3-2017-06","paper":3,"year":"2017","label":"June 2017","num":"06","marks":24,"type":"24","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"The nature of KMH plc's target market is probably the biggest influence on its marketing mix. To what extent is the nature of the target market the most important influence on the marketing mix of all businesses?"},{"id":"P1-2018-18","paper":1,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"18","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"Table showing annual labour turnover rates for BBB plc and its competitors across four time periods","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"The table below shows the changes in the average annual labour turnover rates for BBB plc and its competitors. \nTime period | Annual labour turnover (%) (average for BBB plc) | Annual labour turnover (%) (average for competitors) \n1978–1987: 15, 15; 1988–1997: 12, 18; 1998–2007: 10, 18; 2008–2017: 8, 23 \nAnalyse how the changes in these data over time might have affected the ability of BBB plc to provide higher-quality products than its competitors."},{"id":"P1-2018-19","paper":1,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"19","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how introducing intrapreneurship can improve the financial performance of a business."},{"id":"P1-2018-20","paper":1,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"20","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how delayering might affect the level of profit of a business."},{"id":"P1-2018-21","paper":1,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"21","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"Evaluate the extent to which the use of stakeholder mapping can help the managers of a public limited company to manage change more effectively."},{"id":"P1-2018-22","paper":1,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"22","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"A UK business has experienced slow growth in sales in recent years. It has decided to achieve higher growth through new product development. Do you believe that this is a more risky strategy than market development? Justify your view."},{"id":"P1-2018-23","paper":1,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"23","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"To what extent do you think that UK businesses will experience a fall in profit if governments limit free trade by adopting more protectionist policies?"},{"id":"P1-2018-24","paper":1,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"24","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"Are demographic factors now more significant than economic factors in influencing the performance of UK businesses? Justify your view."},{"id":"P2-2018-01.3","paper":2,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"01.3","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"Appendix A","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Calculate the following ratios for Marks and Spencer plc for the financial year ending 1 April 2017 to two decimal places. The return on capital employed Workings The gearing ratio Workings The current ratio Workings"},{"id":"P2-2018-01.5","paper":2,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"01.5","marks":16,"type":"16d","needs":"Appendices A to F","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"In April 2017 a rival business was considering taking over Marks and Spencer plc. How useful do you think the data provided in Appendices A to F might have been to this rival business when deciding whether to make a take-over bid? Justify your answer."},{"id":"P2-2018-02.1","paper":2,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"02.1","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Lego is a private limited company. Analyse how the decisions its managers make might be different if it was a public limited company."},{"id":"P2-2018-02.2","paper":2,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"02.2","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse the actions managers at Lego might take to help ensure that its employees share the culture of the business."},{"id":"P2-2018-02.3","paper":2,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"02.3","marks":16,"type":"16o","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Lego's profits depend partly on exchange rate changes. To what extent do you think managers of all businesses need to worry about the impact of exchange rates on profits?"},{"id":"P2-2018-03.2","paper":2,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"03.2","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"Appendix G","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Lewin's force field analysis identifies driving and restraining forces. Analyse one driving force and one restraining force in Appendix G for the proposed change to the pay levels for cabin crew."},{"id":"P2-2018-03.3","paper":2,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"03.3","marks":16,"type":"16o","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"To what extent do you think it is essential for an airline to undertake contingency planning?"},{"id":"P3-2018-01","paper":3,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"01","marks":12,"type":"12","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse two benefits to Hopps Clothing Ltd of creating a strong brand."},{"id":"P3-2018-02","paper":3,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"02","marks":12,"type":"12","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse the value of effective inventory control to Hopps Clothing Ltd."},{"id":"P3-2018-03","paper":3,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"03","marks":16,"type":"16","needs":"Appendix B, the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Using the data in Appendix B and the case study, evaluate whether Jack is likely to meet the deadline for his new range."},{"id":"P3-2018-04","paper":3,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"04","marks":16,"type":"16","needs":"Appendix A, the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"In his first year, Jack only used e-commerce instead of distributing through a retailer. To what extent was this a good choice? You should support your answer using Appendix A and the case study."},{"id":"P3-2018-05","paper":3,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"05","marks":20,"type":"20","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Considering both quantitative and qualitative factors, should Jack give up his job to become a full-time entrepreneur? Justify your answer."},{"id":"P3-2018-06","paper":3,"year":"2018","label":"June 2018","num":"06","marks":24,"type":"24","needs":"","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Jack plans to grow his business rapidly over the next few years. To what extent is it possible for businesses to overcome the problems caused by rapid growth?"},{"id":"P1-2019-18","paper":1,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"18","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"Figure 4","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"The Marketing Manager of a business is considering whether to choose Option A or Option B. \nOption A: Introduce a new product. \nOption B: Use a new promotion for an existing product. \nFigure 4 shows the results of a decision tree for these options and the 'do nothing' option. \nFigure 4: A decision tree showing three options. Option A (Introduce a new product) has two outcomes: Success (probability and financial value indicated) and Failure (probability and financial value indicated). Option B (Use a new promotion for an existing product) has two outcomes: Success and Failure. A 'Do nothing' option is also shown with a single outcome value. The expected monetary values are calculated for each option. \nBased on this decision tree, the Marketing Manager chooses Option A. \nUsing Figure 4, analyse why choosing Option A might not be the best decision. \n[9 marks]"},{"id":"P1-2019-19","paper":1,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"19","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"To fund a new project, a business increases the proportion of its long-term funding that is debt. Analyse how this change might affect the level of dividends received by shareholders. \n[9 marks]"},{"id":"P1-2019-20","paper":1,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"20","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Managers in a business have a range of leadership styles. \nAnalyse how these different leadership styles might impact the effectiveness of a strategy to decentralise this business. \n[9 marks]"},{"id":"P1-2019-21","paper":1,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"21","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"Online sales have grown significantly in recent years. To what extent has this led to distribution (place) decisions becoming a more important element of an effective marketing mix?"},{"id":"P1-2019-22","paper":1,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"22","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"A competitive advantage can be achieved through low-cost or through differentiation. Which of these types of competitive advantage is it easier for a UK business to maintain? Justify your view."},{"id":"P1-2019-23","paper":1,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"23","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"More businesses are now using broad measures of overall business performance, such as Kaplan & Norton's Balanced Scorecard and Elkington's Triple Bottom Line, rather than focusing solely on financial ratio analysis. To what extent does this mean that financial ratio analysis is no longer important to a business?"},{"id":"P1-2019-24","paper":1,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"24","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"A business plans to improve its flexibility through mass customisation. Is it inevitable that improved flexibility will worsen other measures of its operational performance? Justify your view."},{"id":"P2-2019-01.4","paper":2,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"01.4","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"Appendix A","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how the combined market share of the largest four manufacturers in the UK RTE breakfast cereal market might affect the threat of entry by other businesses into this market."},{"id":"P2-2019-01.5","paper":2,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"01.5","marks":16,"type":"16d","needs":"Appendices A to E","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Kellogg's is developing a new RTE breakfast cereal for the UK and has examined the market research data in Appendices A to E. Do you think that the use of this market research will guarantee that this new product achieves high sales? Justify your answer."},{"id":"P2-2019-02.1","paper":2,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"02.1","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"WR has made a strategic decision to move into electric bicycle rentals. Analyse the possible impact of this on the market capitalisation of the company."},{"id":"P2-2019-02.2","paper":2,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"02.2","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"WR employs its taxi drivers on flexible employment contracts. Analyse one advantage and one disadvantage of this for the business."},{"id":"P2-2019-02.3","paper":2,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"02.3","marks":16,"type":"16o","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Stricter laws have affected WR's taxi business. To what extent do you think that legal changes create more threats than opportunities for businesses?"},{"id":"P2-2019-03.1","paper":2,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"03.1","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Galin: • invests in research and development • owns a number of patents. Analyse how these two factors help Galin to achieve high profit margins on its new products."},{"id":"P2-2019-03.2","paper":2,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"03.2","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse why Galin has chosen a regional organisational structure rather than a functional one."},{"id":"P2-2019-03.3","paper":2,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"03.3","marks":16,"type":"16o","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Galin wants to increase labour productivity. To what extent do you think that attempts by businesses to increase labour productivity will be welcomed by employees?"},{"id":"P3-2019-01","paper":3,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"01","marks":12,"type":"12","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse two possible reasons why Mike introduced a budgeting system for DWS Ltd in 1991."},{"id":"P3-2019-02","paper":3,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"02","marks":12,"type":"12","needs":"Appendix A, the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how setting up the works council may have led to the changes in Human Resource performance data shown in Appendix A."},{"id":"P3-2019-03","paper":3,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"03","marks":16,"type":"16","needs":"Appendix B, the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"In 2010 Mike introduced a new approach to operations in response to competitive pressures (lines 34–40). Using data from Appendix B and the other information provided, evaluate the extent to which this new approach has been successful."},{"id":"P3-2019-04","paper":3,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"04","marks":16,"type":"16","needs":"Appendix D, the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"DWS Ltd is considering investing in solar panels. Using Appendix D calculate the payback period and the Average Rate of Return of this investment. Based on your results and other information, recommend whether DWS Ltd should make this investment. Justify your decision."},{"id":"P3-2019-05","paper":3,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"05","marks":20,"type":"20","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"To what extent does the information provided support the view that Mike is an effective leader?"},{"id":"P3-2019-06","paper":3,"year":"2019","label":"June 2019","num":"06","marks":24,"type":"24","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"DWS Ltd is considering making a major strategic change. To what extent is a SWOT analysis valuable for any business deciding on its future strategy?"},{"id":"P1-2020N-18","paper":1,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"18","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how employing a more diverse workforce might increase the profit of a business."},{"id":"P1-2020N-19","paper":1,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"19","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"table showing receivables days and payables days for Wilson PLC 2018-2019","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"The table below shows the changes in the two efficiency ratios for Wilson PLC, 2018–2019. Table: Receivables days 30 in 2018, 45 in 2019; Payables days 38 in 2018, 43 in 2019. Analyse the implications of these changes for Wilson PLC's cash levels."},{"id":"P1-2020N-20","paper":1,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"20","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse the problems that might arise for a small business from the growth of digital technology."},{"id":"P1-2020N-21","paper":1,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"21","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"'Limited liability benefits all stakeholders of a public limited company.' Do you agree? Justify your view."},{"id":"P1-2020N-22","paper":1,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"22","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"'The growth stage is the most challenging stage of the product life cycle for a business when managing its human resource flow.' Do you agree? Justify your view."},{"id":"P1-2020N-23","paper":1,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"23","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"'To achieve successful innovation, the level of spending on research and development is more important than the organisational culture of a business.' Do you agree? Justify your view."},{"id":"P1-2020N-24","paper":1,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"24","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"A business is changing from a strategic position of low cost to one of differentiation. Will this lead to the business spending more on marketing and less on the operations function? Justify your view."},{"id":"P2-2020N-01.3","paper":2,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"01.3","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"Appendix E","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse the challenges the Human Resource manager faces as a result of the patterns of room bookings in Appendix E."},{"id":"P2-2020N-01.4","paper":2,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"01.4","marks":16,"type":"16d","needs":"Appendix A, Appendix B, Appendix C, Appendix D","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Using the data, recommend whether Drake Hotels PLC should go ahead with the proposed investment. Justify your answer."},{"id":"P2-2020N-02.3","paper":2,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"02.3","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Nari uses a 'Just in Time' approach to manufacturing. Analyse the ways in which this might affect Nari's profits."},{"id":"P2-2020N-02.4","paper":2,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"02.4","marks":16,"type":"16o","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"The managers of a number of Nari's suppliers use Taylor's motivation theory when motivating their employees. To what extent do you think using Taylor's theory would be a good way for all businesses to motivate their employees?"},{"id":"P2-2020N-03.3","paper":2,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"03.3","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"The price elasticity of demand for Zani PLC's products has a value of –0.4. Analyse reasons why the price elasticity of demand for Zani PLC's products might have this value."},{"id":"P2-2020N-03.4","paper":2,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"03.4","marks":16,"type":"16o","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Zani PLC has grown by selling franchises. To what extent is selling franchises a good way for any business to grow?"},{"id":"P3-2020N-01","paper":3,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"01","marks":12,"type":"12","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse the benefits to stakeholders of the rise in the share price of Sunport PLC."},{"id":"P3-2020N-02","paper":3,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"02","marks":12,"type":"12","needs":"Appendix B and Appendix C","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Using Appendix B and Appendix C, analyse why Sunport PLC chose a multi-domestic strategy for its food divisions."},{"id":"P3-2020N-03","paper":3,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"03","marks":16,"type":"16","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"To what extent is changing to cheaper suppliers a good decision for Sunport PLC?"},{"id":"P3-2020N-04","paper":3,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"04","marks":16,"type":"16","needs":"Appendix D and the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Elaine's view is that Personal Care was Sunport PLC's most successful division in Europe in 2019. To what extent do you agree with Elaine's view? You should support your answer using Appendix D and the other information provided."},{"id":"P3-2020N-05","paper":3,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"05","marks":20,"type":"20","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Whereas Martin delegated most decisions, Elaine will make decisions and then tell managers what they have to do. To what extent is this change in leadership style likely to help the company achieve its objective of improving profitability?"},{"id":"P3-2020N-06","paper":3,"year":"2020N","label":"November 2020","num":"06","marks":24,"type":"24","needs":"","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"To what extent does a commitment to Corporate Social Responsibility decrease profit for all businesses?"},{"id":"P1-2022-19","paper":1,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"19","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse why non-profit organisations set financial objectives."},{"id":"P1-2022-20","paper":1,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"20","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how widening a manager's span of control might affect labour productivity within the department she manages."},{"id":"P1-2022-21","paper":1,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"21","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse why a business might choose to use labour intensive processes rather than capital intensive processes."},{"id":"P1-2022-22","paper":1,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"22","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"To what extent might the use of the Boston Matrix enable a multi-product business to achieve overall sales growth?"},{"id":"P1-2022-23","paper":1,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"23","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"Will the increased use of e-commerce lead to all retailers operating only online? Justify your view."},{"id":"P1-2022-24","paper":1,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"24","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"Evaluate the extent to which the actions of the finance function of a business can help that business to achieve the lowest cost in its market."},{"id":"P1-2022-25","paper":1,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"25","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"Businesses using flexible employment contracts can be criticised for being unethical. To what extent should businesses avoid the use of flexible employment contracts?"},{"id":"P2-2022-01.4","paper":2,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"01.4","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"Appendix C","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how the data in Appendix C will affect how this business might change the price it charges for each type of tea to increase its sales revenue."},{"id":"P2-2022-01.5","paper":2,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"01.5","marks":16,"type":"16d","needs":"Appendix A, Appendix B, Appendix C, Appendix D","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"To what extent does the information provided suggest that now is a good time to launch a new brand of tea?"},{"id":"P2-2022-02.3","paper":2,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"02.3","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"With reference to Maslow's theory, analyse the possible impact of this venture on the motivation of senior managers of the two businesses."},{"id":"P2-2022-02.4","paper":2,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"02.4","marks":16,"type":"16o","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Are ventures a good way for all businesses to grow? Justify your view."},{"id":"P2-2022-03.5","paper":2,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"03.5","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how contingency planning might have helped DT maintain its competitiveness."},{"id":"P2-2022-03.6","paper":2,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"03.6","marks":16,"type":"16o","needs":"","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Reliability is the most important factor in a business' choice of supplier. To what extent is this true for all businesses?"},{"id":"P3-2022-01","paper":3,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"01","marks":12,"type":"12","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse the factors affecting SSN Ltd's promotional decisions."},{"id":"P3-2022-02","paper":3,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"02","marks":12,"type":"12","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how copyright may have been important to the growth of SSN Ltd."},{"id":"P3-2022-03","paper":3,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"03","marks":16,"type":"16","needs":"Appendix C, the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Using information from Appendix C and the case study, recommend whether the use of debt factoring is a good way for SSN Ltd to improve its cash flow."},{"id":"P3-2022-04","paper":3,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"04","marks":16,"type":"16","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"To what extent might SSN Ltd benefit from changing its power culture to a role culture?"},{"id":"P3-2022-05","paper":3,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"05","marks":20,"type":"20","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"To what extent would the reactions of SSN Ltd's stakeholders to the possible takeover be likely to lead to conflict between those stakeholders?"},{"id":"P3-2022-06","paper":3,"year":"2022","label":"June 2022","num":"06","marks":24,"type":"24","needs":"","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"'Without strategic planning all businesses are doomed to fail.' To what extent do you agree with this statement?"},{"id":"P1-2023-18","paper":1,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"18","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse why a large business might choose to introduce a product into a niche market."},{"id":"P1-2023-19","paper":1,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"19","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"Table 2","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"A company sells a single product: Product A. \nTable 2 Income and price elasticity of demand for Product A: Income elasticity of demand +0.5; Price elasticity of demand –2.0 \nDuring the next year: \n• consumer incomes fall \n• the price of Product A increases. \nBased solely on the information provided above, analyse how the sales revenue for Product A will change over the next year."},{"id":"P1-2023-20","paper":1,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"20","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"A business has recently experienced a decline in its level of sales. This led to some redundancies. \nAnalyse how an understanding of Maslow's hierarchy of needs might help this business to motivate its remaining employees."},{"id":"P1-2023-21","paper":1,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"21","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"Many businesses use contingency planning to prepare for major threats. Some of these contingency plans work well, but others fail to protect the business. To what extent is the success of a contingency plan for a major threat more dependent on internal factors than external factors?"},{"id":"P1-2023-22","paper":1,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"22","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"Is it inevitable that large, growing businesses will eventually experience rising unit costs? Justify your view."},{"id":"P1-2023-23","paper":1,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"23","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"'Emerging economies are beneficial to UK businesses, but only as potential markets to help UK businesses to achieve growth.' Do you agree? Justify your view."},{"id":"P1-2023-24","paper":1,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"24","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"A business decides to make increasing profits its main objective. Is it inevitable that this business will need to improve its quality to achieve this objective? Justify your view."},{"id":"P2-2023-01.3","paper":2,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"01.3","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"Appendix A, Appendix D, the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse why AJS plc has decided to become more capital intensive."},{"id":"P2-2023-01.4","paper":2,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"01.4","marks":16,"type":"16d","needs":"Appendix A, Appendix B, Appendix C, Appendix D, Appendix E, the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"With reference to the data provided, would you advise a potential investor to buy shares in AJS plc? Justify your view."},{"id":"P2-2023-02.3","paper":2,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"02.3","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"The role of a manager has different elements. Analyse the impact of the increase in homeworking by office staff on the way that their managers fulfil their role."},{"id":"P2-2023-02.4","paper":2,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"02.4","marks":16,"type":"16o","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Would increased homeworking improve the performance of businesses that use Elkington's Triple Bottom Line to measure their success? Justify your view."},{"id":"P2-2023-03.3","paper":2,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"03.3","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Simply Bake plc decided to remove palm oil from its products. With reference to Lewin's force field analysis, analyse why this decision was made."},{"id":"P2-2023-03.4","paper":2,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"03.4","marks":16,"type":"16o","needs":"","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"'Businesses will never act in a socially responsible way unless they are forced to do so by governments.' To what extent is this true for all businesses?"},{"id":"P3-2023-01","paper":3,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"01","marks":12,"type":"12","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse why Logger Boards Ltd prioritises meeting environmental objectives when making operational decisions."},{"id":"P3-2023-02","paper":3,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"02","marks":12,"type":"12","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Logger Boards Ltd's growth has been organic rather than external. Analyse why Bodhi may have preferred organic growth to external growth."},{"id":"P3-2023-03","paper":3,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"03","marks":16,"type":"16","needs":"Appendix A","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"To what extent does the data in Appendix A suggest that building the new production facility will improve Logger Boards Ltd's operational efficiency?"},{"id":"P3-2023-04","paper":3,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"04","marks":16,"type":"16","needs":"Appendix C, the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"If the new production facility is built, Bodhi will aim to increase sales. To what extent is Bodhi likely to be able to increase sales using his current approach to promotion? Use Appendix C and other information to justify your answer."},{"id":"P3-2023-05","paper":3,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"05","marks":20,"type":"20","needs":"Appendix B, the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Logger Boards Ltd has been offered a bank loan at 5% interest per year for the £500 000 needed to finance the building of its new production facility. Using Appendix B and other information, to what extent is using a bank loan too big a risk for the business? Use quantitative and qualitative information to justify your view."},{"id":"P3-2023-06","paper":3,"year":"2023","label":"June 2023","num":"06","marks":24,"type":"24","needs":"","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Many businesses have a strategy of growth. To what extent does the success of a growth strategy for any business depend mainly on its leadership?"},{"id":"P1-2024-18","paper":1,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"18","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse why a public limited company might prefer to use share capital as a source of finance, rather than a bank loan."},{"id":"P1-2024-19","paper":1,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"19","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse why an underperforming business with a role culture might choose to move towards a power culture."},{"id":"P1-2024-20","paper":1,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"20","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"A UK manufacturer is highly geared and exports 60% of its output. \nAnalyse the impact of a significant increase in UK interest rates on this business."},{"id":"P1-2024-21","paper":1,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"21","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"To what extent are financial ratios the best way of assessing the performance of non-profit organisations, such as charities or mutuals?"},{"id":"P1-2024-22","paper":1,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"22","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"A business changes its human resource management (HRM) approach from hard HRM to soft HRM. To what extent is this change guaranteed to increase the motivation of all employees?"},{"id":"P1-2024-23","paper":1,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"23","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"To what extent does rapid change in the external environment mean that strategic drift is inevitable for a business?"},{"id":"P1-2024-24","paper":1,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"24","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"Will the introduction of lean production always lead to lower unit costs? Justify your view."},{"id":"P2-2024-01.3","paper":2,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"01.3","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"Appendix B","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how the changes in Biggs Ltd's labour productivity, shown in Appendix B, may cause its market share to fall."},{"id":"P2-2024-01.4","paper":2,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"01.4","marks":16,"type":"16d","needs":"Appendices C, D, E and the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"In 2024, Biggs Ltd became the sponsor of a major televised sporting competition that attracts a wide range of ages and is popular with families. With reference to the information provided, evaluate whether Biggs Ltd's decision to promote its new product range in this way is a good idea."},{"id":"P2-2024-02.1","paper":2,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"02.1","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"When introducing its paid service, Soundcheck plc changed its positioning strategy from position 1 to position 4 on Bowman's strategic clock. Analyse why Soundcheck plc decided to change its positioning strategy."},{"id":"P2-2024-02.2","paper":2,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"02.2","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Soundcheck plc has set a corporate objective to achieve an annual profit in 2024. Analyse the difficulties Soundcheck plc may experience when attempting to turn its 2023 loss into a profit in 2024."},{"id":"P2-2024-02.3","paper":2,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"02.3","marks":16,"type":"16o","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Soundcheck plc's management has had good relationships with trade unions and its staff have been supportive of strategic change. To what extent does consultation with trade unions enable all businesses to overcome resistance to strategic change?"},{"id":"P2-2024-03.1","paper":2,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"03.1","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how WWH Ltd could improve its cashflow."},{"id":"P2-2024-03.2","paper":2,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"03.2","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"WWH Ltd's directors are considering making and selling a portfolio of products rather than a single product, in order to increase growth. Analyse how WWH Ltd's organisational design may change if the directors decide to do this."},{"id":"P2-2024-03.3","paper":2,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"03.3","marks":16,"type":"16o","needs":"","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"'Legislation to protect the environment is always damaging to business.' To what extent do you agree this is true for all businesses?"},{"id":"P3-2024-01","paper":3,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"01","marks":12,"type":"12","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how Speed-e-Puds Ltd benefits from operating with a high level of capacity utilisation."},{"id":"P3-2024-02","paper":3,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"02","marks":12,"type":"12","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Sanjay has a marketing objective of achieving a 15% market share within 3 years. Analyse the factors that influenced Sanjay's decision to set his marketing objective at a 15% market share."},{"id":"P3-2024-03","paper":3,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"03","marks":16,"type":"16","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Should Sanjay add 'slushy' machines to his three branches? Use quantitative and qualitative information and calculations to support your answer."},{"id":"P3-2024-04","paper":3,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"04","marks":16,"type":"16","needs":"Appendix C, the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"To what extent is Sanjay's use of SWOT analysis likely to help his strategic planning? Use information from Appendix C and the other information provided to justify your answer."},{"id":"P3-2024-05","paper":3,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"05","marks":20,"type":"20","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Sanjay is considering two options for the growth of Speed-e-Puds Ltd. Would you advise him to choose Option 1 or Option 2? Justify your answer."},{"id":"P3-2024-06","paper":3,"year":"2024","label":"June 2024","num":"06","marks":24,"type":"24","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"A key feature of Sanjay's business is differentiation provided by his innovative, speedy waffle maker. To what extent is successful innovation essential for all businesses choosing a strategy of differentiation?"},{"id":"P1-2025-18","paper":1,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"18","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the table showing changes to the structure of Newtown plc","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"The table below shows changes to the structure of Newtown plc. \nTable: Number of staff 3906 before 2024, 3616 in 2024 onwards; Average span of control 5 before 2024, 15 in 2024 onwards; Levels of hierarchy 6 before 2024, 4 in 2024 onwards. \nAnalyse how this restructuring of Newtown plc in 2024 might affect its speed of response to customer enquiries."},{"id":"P1-2025-19","paper":1,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"19","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how a government changing its fiscal policy might affect a business which produces healthcare products."},{"id":"P1-2025-20","paper":1,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"20","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how adopting an innovation strategy might affect the human resources function of a business."},{"id":"P1-2025-21","paper":1,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"21","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"A UK business's domestic market has stopped growing. The business has decided to become a multinational corporation. To what extent is this decision likely to increase profits?"},{"id":"P1-2025-22","paper":1,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"22","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"The marketing department of a business wishes to increase its market share in a growing market. To what extent is market research the most important activity of the marketing department in order to achieve this objective?"},{"id":"P1-2025-23","paper":1,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"23","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"'The need to continue investment is the most significant difficulty facing a business which is trying to maintain a competitive advantage.' To what extent do you agree? Justify your view."},{"id":"P1-2025-24","paper":1,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"24","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"'A system of quality assurance will always lead to greater profits than a system of quality control.' Do you agree? Justify your view."},{"id":"P2-2025-01.3","paper":2,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"01.3","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"Appendix D, the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Using Appendix D and the other information available, analyse why SCF chose Option 2. Your answer should include quantitative and qualitative information."},{"id":"P2-2025-01.4","paper":2,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"01.4","marks":16,"type":"16d","needs":"Appendix E, the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"To what extent do the changes in the economic environment create more threats than opportunities for SCF? Use Appendix E and the other information provided in your answer."},{"id":"P2-2025-02.3","paper":2,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"02.3","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Use Herzberg's theory to analyse why Ajinder's plan may not improve motivation levels at Seebus plc."},{"id":"P2-2025-02.4","paper":2,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"02.4","marks":16,"type":"16o","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Seebus plc targets its marketing towards higher income customers. Should all businesses segment their markets based on income? Justify your view."},{"id":"P2-2025-03.1","paper":2,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"03.1","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse why Dodo sets HR objectives in relation to the number of employees and employee engagement."},{"id":"P2-2025-03.2","paper":2,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"03.2","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how Dodo would benefit from being the best in its market for its chosen quality measures."},{"id":"P2-2025-03.3","paper":2,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"03.3","marks":16,"type":"16o","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Using non-current assets as fully as possible is the best way to gain low-cost advantage. To what extent is this true for all low-cost businesses?"},{"id":"P3-2025-01","paper":3,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"01","marks":12,"type":"12","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Use Lewin's force field model to analyse why VBM is making major changes now."},{"id":"P3-2025-02","paper":3,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"02","marks":12,"type":"12","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse the impact of the proposed retrenchment on VBM's marketing activities in Europe."},{"id":"P3-2025-03","paper":3,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"03","marks":16,"type":"16","needs":"Appendix C, the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"VBM's Operations Director believes that the new factory could be opened in a year. Do you agree? Justify your view by using the data in Appendix C and other information provided."},{"id":"P3-2025-04","paper":3,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"04","marks":16,"type":"16","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"VBM has major Human Resource challenges such as: • recruitment and training for the factory in Vietnam • managing redundancies in Europe. Which of these two challenges is likely to be harder to manage effectively? Justify your view."},{"id":"P3-2025-05","paper":3,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"05","marks":20,"type":"20","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"To what extent do you agree that VBM's biggest threat is changes in legislation?"},{"id":"P3-2025-06","paper":3,"year":"2025","label":"June 2025","num":"06","marks":24,"type":"24","needs":"","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Effective capacity management involves ensuring a business has the right level of capacity in the right place to match demand. To what extent is effective capacity management always harder for large, multinational businesses than small businesses?"},{"id":"P1-2026-18","paper":1,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"18","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how an understanding of Maslow's theory of motivation might help a business to lower its labour turnover."},{"id":"P1-2026-19","paper":1,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"19","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"A business has operated with poor cash flow and low profit levels for a number of years. It decides to use debt factoring as a source of finance. Analyse the possible impact of this decision on its cash flow and profit level."},{"id":"P1-2026-20","paper":1,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"20","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"network diagram above","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Use the network diagram above in order to answer the following question: The business needs to reduce the length of the critical path. Analyse why the business should focus on its human resources function in order to reduce the length of the critical path."},{"id":"P1-2026-21","paper":1,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"21","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"'In the market for sports shoes, the product is always the most important element of the marketing mix.' Do you agree? Justify your view."},{"id":"P1-2026-22","paper":1,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"22","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"A car manufacturer wishes to increase its profits. To what extent is vertical integration likely to be a better way for it to achieve increased profits than horizontal integration?"},{"id":"P1-2026-23","paper":1,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"23","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"'Capital-intensive processes are always more profitable than labour-intensive processes.' Do you agree? Justify your view."},{"id":"P1-2026-24","paper":1,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"24","marks":25,"type":"25","needs":"","lab":"marker.html","q":"Are profitability ratios more important to a business than other types of financial ratios, such as liquidity and gearing ratios? Justify your view."},{"id":"P2-2026-01.3","paper":2,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"01.3","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"Appendix C","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Using Appendix C, analyse how Metromart would benefit from effective inventory control."},{"id":"P2-2026-01.4","paper":2,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"01.4","marks":16,"type":"16d","needs":"Appendix D, the information provided","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"More than 90% of Bargain Barn's sales are from its food business. Evaluate whether offering a wider range of goods and services is likely to be an effective way for Bargain Barn to increase its operating profit margin. Use Appendix D and the other information provided in your answer."},{"id":"P2-2026-02.1","paper":2,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"02.1","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how QWV could measure its business performance."},{"id":"P2-2026-02.2","paper":2,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"02.2","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how being a social enterprise could provide QWV with a competitive advantage."},{"id":"P2-2026-02.3","paper":2,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"02.3","marks":16,"type":"16o","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Increased government legislation in recent years has had an impact on QWV's activities. To what extent is an increase in government legislation bad for all businesses?"},{"id":"P2-2026-03.1","paper":2,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"03.1","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how Shortcut UK's regional organisational structure could lead its business customers to become brand loyal."},{"id":"P2-2026-03.2","paper":2,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"03.2","marks":9,"type":"9","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse why Shortcut may have found the UK an attractive market to target."},{"id":"P2-2026-03.3","paper":2,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"03.3","marks":16,"type":"16o","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Would using performance-related pay be beneficial for all businesses? Justify your decision."},{"id":"P3-2026-01","paper":3,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"01","marks":12,"type":"12","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how Danni's customers may be affected by his decision to change from operating as a sole trader to becoming a private limited company."},{"id":"P3-2026-02","paper":3,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"02","marks":12,"type":"12","needs":"the case study","lab":"nine_marker_lab.html","q":"Analyse how using network analysis can help Danni to ensure customer satisfaction."},{"id":"P3-2026-03","paper":3,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"03","marks":16,"type":"16","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Should Danni increase his employees' wages by 20% or not? Justify your view."},{"id":"P3-2026-04","paper":3,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"04","marks":16,"type":"16","needs":"Appendix E","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"To what extent are the economic forecasts in Appendix E positive for Danni's business?"},{"id":"P3-2026-05","paper":3,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"05","marks":20,"type":"20","needs":"Appendix C, Appendix D","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Managing cash flow is more important than making profit for Danni's business. To what extent do you agree? Use information from Appendix C and Appendix D within your answer."},{"id":"P3-2026-06","paper":3,"year":"2026","label":"June 2026","num":"06","marks":24,"type":"24","needs":"the case study","lab":"open_essay_lab.html","q":"Danni's suppliers import many of their products from businesses located in China and other East Asian countries. Should all UK businesses try to use only UK suppliers?"}];
